; resize_leaves_variables_outside_the_grid: the extent bound is `<=`, not
; `==`.
;
; EQUALITY, ATLEAST, ATLEASTW and REDUCE append slack and auxiliary
; variables past the grid, and nothing ever shrinks a register's size, so
; a model whose size exceeds its extent is the normal state after any of
; them. A later RESIZE over a strict subset of the variables must still be
; accepted.

PUSH 10
BQMX r0

PUSH 2           ; rows
PUSH 3           ; cols -- 6 cells over 10 declared variables
RESIZE r0

PUSH 1           ; row
ROWSUM r0
HALT
